  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Interracial Marriage",
  "description": "The meme references the idea that 'too many of our brothers are not marrying our sisters,' which is a racially coded statement implying that Black women are not desirable or 'good enough' for interracial unions. This stereotype suggests that Black women are inferior or less desirable when compared to white women, and that their value is diminished if they do not marry within their own race. This is a form of racial discrimination that targets Black women specifically.",
